{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Electric Vehicle Sales Data Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook explores the electric vehicle sales data across different states in India."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Import necessary libraries\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set visualization styles\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-whitegrid')\n",
    "sns.set_palette('viridis')\n",
    "%matplotlib inline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data Loading\n",
    "\n",
    "Load the raw data from the data directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Define the path to the data file\n",
    "# Update this path to your actual data file\n",
    "data_path = '../data/raw/ev_sales_data.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load the data\n",
    "# If your data is in a different format, adjust accordingly\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "    print(f\"Data loaded successfully with {df.shape[0]} rows and {df.shape[1]} columns.\")\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"File not found: {data_path}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please place your data file in the correct location or update the path.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine the structure and content of the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Display the first few rows of the dataset\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    display(df.head())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check data information\n",
    "    print(\"\\nData Information:\")\n",
    "    df.info()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check summary statistics\n",
    "    print(\"\\nSummary Statistics:\")\n",
    "    display(df.describe())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check for missing values\n",
    "    print(\"\\nMissing Values:\")\n",
    "    missing_values = df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "    display(missing_values[missing_values > 0])\n",
    "except NameError:\n",
    "    print(\"Data not loaded. Please ensure the data file exists.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's explore the data to understand the patterns and relationships."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Example: Distribution of EV sales by state\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "    # Assuming 'State' and 'Sales' columns exist - adjust as needed\n",
    "    sns.barplot(x='State', y='Sales', data=df)\n",
    "    plt.title('Electric Vehicle Sales by State')\n",
    "    plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "except (NameError, KeyError) as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please adjust the column names to match your actual data.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Example: Time series analysis of sales (if time data is available)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    # Assuming 'Date' and 'Sales' columns exist - adjust as needed\n",
    "    if 'Date' in df.columns:\n",
    "        df['Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date'])\n",
    "        time_series = df.groupby(df['Date'].dt.to_period('M')).agg({'Sales': 'sum'}).reset_index()\n",
    "        time_series['Date'] = time_series['Date'].dt.to_timestamp()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        plt.figure(figsize=(14, 6))\n",
    "        plt.plot(time_series['Date'], time_series['Sales'], marker='o')\n",
    "        plt.title('Monthly Electric Vehicle Sales Trend')\n",
    "        plt.xlabel('Month')\n",
    "        plt.ylabel('Total Sales')\n",
    "        plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "        plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "        plt.show()\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"No 'Date' column found for time series analysis.\")\n",
    "except (NameError, KeyError) as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please adjust the column names to match your actual data.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Correlation Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine the relationships between different variables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Example: Correlation heatmap\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    # Select only numeric columns\n",
    "    numeric_df = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Calculate correlation matrix\n",
    "    corr_matrix = numeric_df.corr()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot correlation heatmap\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "    sns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "    plt.title('Correlation Matrix of Numeric Features')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "except NameError:\n",
    "    print(\"Data not loaded. Please ensure the data file exists.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on this initial exploration, the next steps would be:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Data cleaning and preprocessing\n",
    "2. Feature engineering\n",
    "3. Model development\n",
    "4. Model evaluation\n",
    "5. Insights and recommendations"
   ]
  }
 ],
